      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This phenomenon is often related to the use of \"filler phrases\" or transitional jargon in public speaking. These predictable phrases help maintain a professional, authoritative tone and create a sense of rhythm in structured media appearances. It can also serve as rhetorical scaffolding, allowing speakers to pivot between complex ideas smoothly without losing audience engagement. Essentially, these set phrases function as linguistic shortcuts to signal control and forward momentum during scripted communication.",
